  The cited fact is supported. The port-layer energy identity follows from multiplying the four port equations by E, W_x, W_y, and P_t/kappa, using tau P_t + P = kappa E to convert E P_t into the P-energy derivative plus tau kappa^{-1} P_t^2, and using the Maxwell cross-term divergence identity. The planar x-PML Laplace-Fourier calculation gives the stated Y_port^2 - Y_0^2 formula, and its oblique k_y term cannot be removed by any scalar local sigma_E independent of frequency and tangential wavenumber. With all damping zero, the equations reduce to Maxwell-Debye after W_x=H_x and W_y=H_y.

